The `generateRandomString` method should accept two parameters: an integer `$length` representing the desired length of the generated string and a string `$charset` representing the character set to be used for generating the random string. This method should return a randomly generated string based on the provided length and character set.

The `executeDatabaseQuery` method should accept a byte array `$inputBytes` as input, establish a connection to a database server using a provided connection string, and execute a query with the input bytes as a parameter. The method should then return a `mysqli_result` object containing the result of the query.

Below is the implementation of the `SecureDataHandler` class:

```php
class SecureDataHandler
{
    public function generateRandomString($length, $charset)
    {
        $randomString = '';
        $charsetLength = strlen($charset);
        for ($i = 0; $i < $length; $i++) {
            $randomString .= $charset[rand(0, $charsetLength - 1)];
        }
        return $randomString;
    }

    public function executeDatabaseQuery($inputBytes)
    {
        $connectionString = "YourConnectionStringHere";
        $query = "SELECT * FROM YourTableName WHERE someColumn = @inputParam";
        $dbConnection = new mysqli("localhost", "username", "password", "databaseName");
        if ($dbConnection->connect_error) {
            die("Connection failed: " . $dbConnection->connect_error);
        }
        $stmt = $dbConnection->prepare($query);
        $stmt->bind_param("b", $inputBytes);
        $stmt->execute();
        return $stmt->get_result();
    }
}
