```java
import java.io.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class ShellCommandExecutor {
    private ExecutorService executor;
    private BlockingQueue<Runnable> commandQueue;

    public ShellCommandExecutor(int maxThreads) {
        this.executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(maxThreads);
        this.commandQueue = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>();
    }

    public void executeCommand(String command, String directory) throws InterruptedException {
        CommandTask task = new CommandTask(command, directory);
        commandQueue.put(task);
        executor.execute(task);
    }

    private class CommandTask implements Runnable {
        private String command;
        private String directory;

        public CommandTask(String command, String directory) {
            this.command = command;
            this.directory = directory;
        }

        @Override
        public void run() {
            Process process = null;
            try {
                ProcessBuilder pb = new ProcessBuilder("/bin/bash", "-c", command);
                if (directory != null && !directory.isEmpty()) {
                    pb.directory(new File(directory));
                }
                process = pb.start();

                // Capture stdout and stderr
                Thread outputThread = new Thread(() -> readStream(process.getInputStream()));
                Thread errorThread = new Thread(() -> readStream(process.getErrorStream()));
                outputThread.start();
                errorThread.start();

                int exitCode = process.waitFor();
                if (exitCode != 0) {
                    System.err.println("Command failed with exit code: " + exitCode);
                }
            } catch (IOException | InterruptedException e) {
                e.printStackTrace();
            } finally {
                if (process != null && process.isAlive()) {
                    process.destroy();
                }
            }
        }

        private void readStream(InputStream stream) {
            try (BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(stream))) {
                String line;
                while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                    System.out.println(line);
                }
            } catch (IOException e) {
                e.printStackTrace();
            }
        }
    }

    public void shutdown() {
        executor.shutdown();
    }
}
```

This code snippet provides a basic implementation of a `ShellCommandExecutor` class in Java. The class uses an `ExecutorService` to manage multiple concurrent processes and a `BlockingQueue` to queue commands for execution. The `executeCommand` method allows submitting commands with optional custom directories.

The `CommandTask` inner class represents the actual task that executes a shell command. It configures a `ProcessBuilder` with the provided command and directory, starts the process, captures both stdout and stderr in separate threads, waits for the process to complete, and handles any exceptions or errors.

To use this utility, you can create an instance of `ShellCommandExecutor` with a specified number of threads (e.g., 10), and then call `executeCommand` with the desired shell command and optional directory. The utility will manage concurrency, resource cleanup, and basic error handling for each command execution.

